WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.420
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:08.390
Tell us the story of how 
Yusaku and Kusanagi met!

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.590
Leave this to me.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.980
Log out!

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.560
Why do you oppose us?

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.470
Do you know about the Lost Incident?

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.970
Unknown is also investigating 
the Lost Incident.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:37.000
When you saved me, I could envision 
my brother growing strong like you.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.940
Please team up with me!

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.940
If you're the strongest spear 
to fight the Knights of Hanoi...

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.660
...I'll be the strongest 
shield to protect you!

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:11.360
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:18.150
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:25.470
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:32.050
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:38.790
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:46.030
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:52.730
I want to share your pain

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:31.430
Watch out!

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.140
Are you okay, Unnamed?

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.870
Sorry, Unknown.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:50.160
Whoever created this dungeon 
watched too many movies.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:54.500
Even though we're in VR, I would've 
taken big damage in real life.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.220
That's if you're lucky.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:02.460
If you leave your Duel Disk 
here, you can't log out.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.160
This is no ordinary dungeon.

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:10.900
Unknown, is there really something 
deep inside this dungeon?

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:14.160
We won't know until we get there.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:30.000
Despite how many Knights of Hanoi we 
defeat, the minions don't have much info.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:33.720
There's no point talking to them.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:38.960
They initiate duels by 
claiming to hunt the Cyberse.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.200
I know we have to keep fighting, but...

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.160
It's normal to feel impatient.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.410
What are you investigating?

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:54.220
I found a website about 
a Cyberse urban legend.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.610
Urban legend?

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:59.320
When the Hanoi hunted the 
Cyberse, someone got scared.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:03.590
So it says he built a dungeon 
containing a Cyberse Deck.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.900
Laughable, right?

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.000
I never thought about that.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.980
Why the Knights of Hanoi hunt the Cyberse.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:17.060
Is it because they're afraid of the Cyberse?

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:25.280
If there really is a Cyberse Deck, it may 
be the secret weapon against the Hanoi.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.560
Let's go!

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.100
Are you serious?

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.150
The secret dungeon is real.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:40.390
So it's very likely that 
it contains a Cyberse Deck.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:45.620
But all this info could be a 
trap by the Knights of Hanoi.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.500
If it's a trap, that's fine.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:54.240
Our ultimate goal is to find the Knights of 
Hanoi and learn the truth about the Lost Incident.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:59.520
So if the Hanoi stand in our 
way, I'll gladly fight them.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:07.950
But if the info is real and we acquire the 
Cyberse Deck, the Hanoi will come to us.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.060
Saving us the trouble of finding the Hanoi.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.760
So you've thought that far ahead.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:33.410
The Cyberse Deck must be 
inside that sarcophagus.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:37.150
But how do we get there?

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:41.920
I made it!

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.820
Only I shall achieve this feat!

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.090
A Knight of Hanoi!

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:49.700
They also used the info to get here.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.060
It means this isn't a Hanoi trap.

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:18.170
They're all Cyberse monsters!

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.300
They're going to duel?

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:35.450
But this isn't a chess 
quiz.  It's a duel quiz.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.480
It's the final test to get the reward.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:40.300
This is bad.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:43.210
He'll get the Cyberse Deck before us!

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:46.680
Only if he clears this duel.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.690
This is a difficult quiz.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:52.160
Let's just watch for now.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:56.390
But even if he fails, he'll solve 
it eventually if he keeps trying.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.160
Are you sure?

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:02.370
I don't think whoever created 
this dungeon will be so nice.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:07.840
To solve this duel quiz, he probably 
has to lower the ghost's LP to 0.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:13.810
Yeah.  The ghost has 4000 
LP, and he has 100 LP.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:21.050
On the ghost's field are five Link Monsters 
that have Extra Linked and one set card.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:25.520
This side has two monsters and two set cards.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:29.370
I want to know what cards are in his hand

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:33.670
and are set, but it seems hard 
to eliminate all the ghost's LP.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:37.900
I'll finish this quick.  I draw!

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:42.300
From my hand, I equip 
Megamorph on Update Jammer!

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.140
Its ATK double!

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:51.120
When Update Jammer destroys a monster, 
its effect deals 1000 damage.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.120
Update Jammer now has 4000 ATK.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:59.360
Link Spider has 1000 ATK.  
I can attack it and win!

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.390
This is bad!

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.600
Go, Update Jammer!

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:08.340
Attack Link Spider!

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.310
Chaos Burst?

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:29.190
He set Chaos Burst, which destroys the 
attacking monster and deals 1000 damage.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:33.440
But now that I know, I'll retry 
using a different strategy.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:36.860
What?

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:47.710
Save me!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.920
Like I thought, you only get one chance.

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:09.050
What was that?

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:13.130
I've never seen anyone forced 
to log out like that!

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.340
This is dangerous.  It's no ordinary game.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:22.570
But if we clear this, we may 
acquire the Cyberse Deck.

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:25.580
That's why we came here.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.950
We have to do this.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:33.650
Unknown...

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.070
Duel!

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:50.360
Here I go!  I draw!

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:52.850
I have four cards in my hand.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:58.180
Tremendous Fire, Thunder Crash, 
Megamorph and Cyberse Gadget.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:02.130
On the field are two 
monsters and two set cards.

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:05.430
Update Jammer and Sea Archiver.

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:08.790
The set cards are Link Restart 
and Torrential Reborn.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:13.830
Think carefully.  The hand and field 
aren't the only cards you can use.

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.830
Level 1 Dotscaper is in the graveyard.

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:20.740
There are three Link 
Monsters in the Extra Deck.

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:25.540
Secure Gardna, Binary 
Sorceress and Proxy Dragon.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:30.510
I have 100 LP.  The ghost has 4000 LP.

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:35.750
And he has five Link Monsters 
that have Extra Linked.

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:45.940
When a Cyberse battles, Update Jammer negates 
all other card effects during damage calculation.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:52.150
And if it destroys a monster in 
battle, it deals 1000 damage.

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:57.800
The Knight of Hanoi tried to use this effect.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:00.940
Isn't it weird?

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:06.910
If all other card effects are negated, why 
did he lose due to Chaos Burst's effect?

00:11:07.170 --> 00:11:08.590
It's not weird.

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:12.520
Chaos Burst activated when 
he declared an attack.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:16.750
That's before the timing when Update 
Jammer can activate its effect.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:20.920
Either way, the Knight of Hanoi's 
attempt would've failed.

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:22.460
What do you mean?

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:27.400
Update Jammer not only negates 
your opponent's cards.

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:32.720
Even if he equipped Megamorph, Update 
Jammer would've negated its effect.

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:35.910
So he would've failed to 
erase all his opponent's LP.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:40.140
That's too complicated for me.

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:43.150
It is complicated and difficult.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:44.850
But if we fail...

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:48.320
It you can't attack, how 
about using effect damage?

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:51.290
Three cards deal effect damage.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:56.030
Tremendous Fire, Thunder 
Crash and Torrential Reborn.

00:11:56.030 --> 00:12:01.780
Tremendous Fire deals 1000 damage to the 
opponent, but we'll take damage too.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:06.470
Since we only have 100 LP, 
we can't use this card.

00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:10.810
The remaining two cards can 
deal damage to the ghost.

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:18.520
By destroying all our monsters, Thunder 
Crash deals 300 damage for each one.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:25.990
Torrential Reborn resurrects destroyed 
monsters and deals 500 damage for each one.

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:32.730
I have the Water Attribute Sea Archiver, 
which is required to activate Torrential Reborn.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:37.340
But how can we deal 4000 damage?

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.360
I know!

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:50.060
You went thinking it was an 
urban legend, but it was true!

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:53.540
But they haven't acquired 
the Cyberse Deck yet.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:57.360
They must clear the quiz to know 
if the legend is true or not.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:00.020
So what happened, Kusanagi?

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:01.350
Well...

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.970
I summon Cyberse Gadget!

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:12.810
When it's summoned, I can Special 
Summon a Level 2 or lower monster

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:14.770
from my graveyard in defense position.

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:17.740
Resurrect, Dotscaper!

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:21.210
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.130
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:28.620
The summoning conditions 
are two non-Token monsters!

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:30.590
Link Summon!

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:33.590
Link 2 Binary Sorceress!

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:41.870
Since Cyberse Gadget was sent to the 
graveyard, its effect activates!

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:44.560
I Special Summon a Gadget Token!

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:48.210
Then Dotscaper's effect activates!

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:52.780
When it's sent from the field to the 
graveyard, it Special Summons itself!

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:56.250
Now Unknown has five monsters on his field!

00:13:56.780 --> 00:14:01.850
If he uses Thunder Crash and Torrential 
Reborn, the ghost will have 0 LP!

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:05.170
Next, I Link Summon-

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:08.530
You fool!

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:14.530
If you destroy Gadget Token, Torrential 
Reborn can't resurrect it!

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:17.130
A Knight of Hanoi?  Since when?

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:18.900
You're done!

00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:21.370
The Knights of Hanoi will 
take the Cyberse Deck-

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:22.880
I won't let you!

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:26.180
Unnamed!

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:28.650
You...

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:31.100
Hands off me!

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:34.520
Are you okay?

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:37.980
Yeah.  But it won't last long.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.220
Can you make it?

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:41.190
It's plenty.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:45.660
But Torrential Reborn 
can't resurrect a Token.

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:49.800
Right.  But there's still a path.

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:53.270
The summoning conditions are two monsters!

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:55.080
Link Summon!

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:57.420
Link 2 Proxy Dragon!

00:15:01.010 --> 00:15:02.520
You sure?

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:05.020
You have fewer monsters now.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:08.850
Next, I use Binary Sorceress to Link Summon!

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:13.080
Appear!  Link 1 Secure Gardna!

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:22.600
You summoned all the Link 
Monsters in your Extra Deck.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:24.670
Out of options?

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:27.380
It's over.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:28.820
Giving up?

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:32.200
I'll never give up.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:35.040
Not until I regain my severed past!

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:40.260
Not until we get revenge on 
the ones who made us suffer!

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:42.200
That's right.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:47.280
If we give up, we'll lose our chance to 
learn the truth about the Lost Incident!

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:48.960
We can't let that happen!

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:53.430
Here I go!  I activate Tremendous Fire!

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:58.800
You takes 1000 damage, and I take 500 damage!

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.840
Have you lost your mind?

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:03.110
Now you have 0 LP!

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:05.080
Unknown!

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:10.080
I activate the Counter Trap, Link Restart!

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:15.250
When an effect that deals me damage 
activates, that card is negated.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:18.860
And I Special Summon a Link 
Monster from the graveyard!

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:21.830
Resurrect, Binary Sorceress!

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:27.770
We now have five monsters!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:31.240
I activate the spell card, Thunder Crash!

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:34.970
All monsters on my field are destroyed.

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:38.730
And you take 300 damage for each one!

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:46.120
That's 1500 damage!

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:53.860
And since the Water Attribute Sea Archiver 
was destroyed, Torrential Reborn activates!

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:57.260
All destroyed monsters are Special Summoned.

00:16:57.260 --> 00:17:00.310
And you take 500 damage for each one!

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.870
I resurrect five monsters!

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:06.490
I deal 2500 damage!

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.390
Just a bit more.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:26.660
Oh no!  Let's go!

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:28.590
Stop!

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:38.230
Okay, the Cyberse Deck is inside.

00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:48.810
It was a prank.

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:51.210
What a waste of effort.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:55.390
After all this work, there's nothing?

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:57.620
You must be joking!

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:05.590
Unnamed, let's go!

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:18.040
Hey, it's really nearby?

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:21.050
If my judgment isn't wrong.

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:44.700
The duel quiz was a treasure map.

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:52.700
The final layout mirrored Den City.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:56.940
Three bridges over the 
river: the Trigate Bridge.

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:59.620
The first is currently under construction.

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:04.090
By mirroring the Link Marker gap to this 
bridge, I narrowed it down to this spot.

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:10.160
But if the Link Markers mirror the 
map, other locations are possible too.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:16.200
Yeah.  For the positions of the monsters 
Special Summoned by Torrential Reborn...

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:18.270
...they could've been shuffled.

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:22.740
So this might not be the treasure's location.

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:26.630
When I saw the bridges connecting 
the links, it dawned on me.

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:31.300
And when I Link Summoned 
Secure Gardna, I was certain.

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:35.120
If the bridges only 
symbolize what's linked...

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:41.680
...there had to be a bridge between the 
co-linked Secure Gardna and Proxy Dragon.

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:48.570
So the link connections 
were there to guide us.

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:56.200
And this is the final destination - the 
location where Secure Gardna was summoned.

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:06.460
You're right!  You did it, Yusaku!

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:16.290
This is the strongest deck to fight 
against the Knights of Hanoi.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:21.770
We finally acquired the power to get revenge!

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:25.350
This deck symbolizes our bond.

00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:29.220
As long as we have this 
deck, our bond is eternal!

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:34.750
So that's how you acquired the Cyberse Deck.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.980
But there's still a question unanswered.

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:38.880
Yeah.

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:42.690
He hasn't become Playmaker yet.

00:20:44.480 --> 00:20:46.000
You're right.

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:52.360
I know your secret.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:57.270
Hey, Playmaker...

00:20:57.970 --> 00:21:01.020
...is my soulmate, right?

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:05.080
And since you're my best friend, 
you should feel proud too!

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:07.040
What do you want to talk about?

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:09.510
I know you have a part-time job.

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:14.200
I saw you working at the hot dog stand.

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:20.220
The school forbids working part-time jobs, 
but I'm not so petty to snitch on you.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:21.190
However...

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:25.660
Help me fill out postcards to enter 
Blue Angel's handshake event-

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:30.020
Hey, Fujiki!

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:33.400
I'll snitch you out to Playmaker!

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:39.910
I still remember that day.

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:44.640
We made a vow to declare war on the Hanoi.

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:48.520
Unknown will be the commander 
to fight the Hanoi!

00:21:50.150 --> 00:21:51.260
Damn!

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:53.720
Who are you?

00:21:56.690 --> 00:21:58.960
My name is Playmaker.

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:02.750
The envoy of revenge that 
fights the Knights of Hanoi!

00:22:19.870 --> 00:22:26.210
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:32.910
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:33.340 --> 00:22:36.410
Memories left behind  Erased memories

00:22:36.410 --> 00:22:39.550
What was the PASSWORD again?

00:22:39.980 --> 00:22:44.150
ACCESS records  Restored memories

00:22:44.420 --> 00:22:47.120
Challenge "the you inside you"

00:22:51.830 --> 00:22:58.000
You're a Network  The 
World that spreads beyond

00:22:58.140 --> 00:23:01.140
With repeating "nows"

00:23:01.470 --> 00:23:05.080
